course: dictionary
lesson: 6055
title: Learning from a mentor
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A mentor is an experienced and trusted person who helps and advises someone younger or less experienced, often over a long time. «My mentor showed me how to plan my stories.» Here mentor is a noun, a person. Mentor can also be a verb, which means to help and guide someone in this way.
explain: Look at the clues around the word. Experienced, trusted, helps and advises tell you that a mentor knows a lot and wants to share it. «Our new teacher has a mentor who visits every Friday.» Visits every Friday tells you the help keeps going over time.
explain: Swap your meaning into the sentence to check it. Could you say «My guide showed me how to plan my stories»? Yes, it still makes sense, so guide is close in meaning. But a mentor is more than a guide: the help lasts, and the person is trusted.
explain: The example sentence shows where some words come from. «Many everyday English words were born in these old stories: panic, odyssey, mentor, echo, cereal and even the month of January.» Mentor comes from an old Greek story, so it has a very long history.
fact: A mentor is an experienced and trusted person who helps and advises a younger or less experienced person over time.
fact: As a verb, «to mentor» means to help and guide someone in this way.
fact: The word comes from Mentor, Odysseus's friend in an old Greek myth, who helped Odysseus's son Telemachus.
fact: Phrases to notice: «a peer mentor», «a mentoring scheme» and «my mentor» all describe someone who helps you learn.
exercise: «Our new teacher has a mentor who visits every Friday.» What is a mentor? | *An experienced person who helps and advises someone | A type of school bag | A loud sound that bounces back | A person who only tests you once
exercise: Priya says, «Mentor is just another word for boss.» Which idea is closer to the true meaning? | A person who is much older than everyone | A person who only plays games with you | *A trusted person who helps and guides you over time | A person who gives orders and never helps
exercise: Which verb means to help and guide someone in the way a mentor does? | sleep | forget | *mentor | shout
test: «My mentor showed me how to plan my stories.» What does this sentence tell you? | *Someone experienced helped and guided the writer over time | Mentor is a kind of pencil | The stories were read out loud at night | The writer lost all her stories
test: Which name belongs to Odysseus's friend in the old Greek myth? | *Mentor | Odysseus | Panic | Telemachus
exam: Which sentence uses mentor as a verb? | The mentors met us at the gate | My mentor is kind and wise | A mentor sat by the window | *Our teacher will mentor the new pupils this year
